<title>UK: INTERVIEW-Williams has lock on credit line.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW-Williams has lock on credit line.</headline>
<byline>Jeff Daeschner</byline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>British security group Williams Holdings Plc said on Friday it had arranged a new five-year credit facility for about 1.0 billion stg to help finance its planned acquisition of Chubb Security Plc.</p>
<p>Williams' 1.3 billion stg bid, recommended by Chubb's board, was composed of about 50 percent stock and 50 percent cash, chief executive Roger Carr told Reuters in an interview.</p>
<p>&quot;This is financed very strongly. We have interest cover of just under 6.0 times, which we are extrememly comfortably with, and cash generative businesses,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
